# The sdist carries what the README tells a reader to read, and what a second
# implementation reads: the trust model, the changelog, the worked policies, the
# format spec and the conformance corpus. Those were absent, so every link out of
# the long description was a dead end for anyone who arrived by `pip install`.
include CHANGELOG.md CONTRIBUTING.md SECURITY.md
graft conformance
graft docs
graft examples
graft policies
graft spec

# The tests do not ship, deliberately. setuptools' default discovery picked up
# `tests/test*.py` from an old distutils glob and nothing else, so the tarball
# carried 40 test modules without conftest.py, the conformance corpus or the policy
# gallery — a suite that died at collection and told a source consumer this release
# cannot verify itself. Making it runnable would mean shipping the repository: the
# suite also reads demo/ and scripts/ from the tree root, and demo/ is five
# applications with their own dependency sets and generated databases. So the
# distribution stops half-shipping a suite; the suite runs against the tag it was
# written for, https://github.com/Szesnasty/histos/tree/v0.1.0.
prune tests

# `src/histos.egg-info` is a gitignored artifact of a previous local build that was
# landing in the tarball — a distribution carrying another build's PKG-INFO and
# requires.txt. `SOURCES.txt` stays: setuptools copies it into the release tree after
# this template is processed, and it describes this build rather than an older one.
prune src/histos.egg-info

global-exclude __pycache__/* *.py[cod] .DS_Store
